cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Predicting rises in family homelessness from published local authority data
message: If you refer to this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mahdi
    family-names: Sabet Kish
    orcid: null
abstract: >-
  A prospective backtest of statistical and machine learning methods for
  identifying English local authorities where homelessness among families with
  dependent children is about to rise, together with a neighbourhood-level
  segmentation and anomaly screen for Colchester. Built entirely on public
  data released under the Open Government Licence.
keywords:
  - homelessness
  - housing insecurity
  - administrative data
  - risk prediction
  - model calibration
  - public sector analytics
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-08"
